-- src:1688 | (a) A close corporation is a corporation organized under this chapter whose certificate of incorporation contains the provisions required by § 102 of this title and, in addition, provides that:
-- src:1689 | (1) All of the corporation’s issued stock of all classes, exclusive of treasury shares, shall be represented by certificates and shall be held of record by not more than a specified number of persons, not exceeding 30; and
-- src:1690 | (2) All of the issued stock of all classes shall be subject to 1 or more of the restrictions on transfer permitted by § 202 of this title; and
-- src:1691 | (3) The corporation shall make no offering of any of its stock of any class which would constitute a “public offering” within the meaning of the United States Securities Act of 1933 [15 U.S.C. § 77a et seq.] as it may be amended from time to time.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 342(a) (src:1688-1691)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 342(a) Certificate of incorporation of a corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 342(a) the corporation is a close corporation` certificate MEANS
        certificate's `the corporation is organized under this chapter`
    AND certificate's `the certificate contains the provisions required by s 102`
    AND `s 342(a) the certificate contains the provisions of paragraphs (1) to (3)` certificate

-- (b): the qualifications of stockholders the certificate may set, by classes of persons entitled or not entitled.
-- src:1692 | (b) The certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may set forth the qualifications of stockholders, either by specifying classes of persons who shall be entitled to be holders of record of stock of any class, or by specifying classes of persons who shall not be entitled to be holders of stock of any class or both.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 342(b) (src:1692)
GIVEN `the certificate specifies classes of persons entitled to be holders of record of stock of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in one of those classes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate specifies classes of persons not entitled to be holders of stock of the class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in one of the classes not entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 342(b) the person is entitled under the certificate to be a holder of record of the stock` `the certificate specifies classes of persons entitled to be holders of record of stock of the class` `the person is in one of those classes` `the certificate specifies classes of persons not entitled to be holders of stock of the class` `the person is in one of the classes not entitled` MEANS
        ((NOT `the certificate specifies classes of persons entitled to be holders of record of stock of the class`) OR `the person is in one of those classes`)
    AND ((NOT `the certificate specifies classes of persons not entitled to be holders of stock of the class`) OR (NOT `the person is in one of the classes not entitled`))

-- (c): stock held in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties is treated as held by 1 stockholder.
-- fork F9: each such tenancy counts as one holder of record.
-- src:1693 | (c) For purposes of determining the number of holders of record of the stock of a close corporation, stock which is held in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties shall be treated as held by 1 stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 342(c) (src:1693)
GIVEN `the number of holders of record who hold stock otherwise than in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of joint or common tenancies and tenancies by the entireties in which stock is held of record` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 342(c) the number of holders of record of the stock` `the number of holders of record who hold stock otherwise than in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties` `the number of joint or common tenancies and tenancies by the entireties in which stock is held of record` MEANS
    `the number of holders of record who hold stock otherwise than in joint or common tenancy or by the entireties` PLUS `the number of joint or common tenancies and tenancies by the entireties in which stock is held of record`

-- The breach the certificate's cap guards against: more holders of record than the number it specifies.
-- src:1689 | (1) All of the corporation’s issued stock of all classes, exclusive of treasury shares, shall be represented by certificates and shall be held of record by not more than a specified number of persons, not exceeding 30; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 342(a)(1) (src:1689)
GIVEN `the number of holders of record` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of persons the certificate specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 342(a)(1) the stock is held of record by more persons than the certificate specifies` `the number of holders of record` `the number of persons the certificate specifies` MEANS
    `the number of holders of record` GREATER THAN `the number of persons the certificate specifies`

