    AND `s 343(1) the certificate of incorporation has the heading the paragraph requires` `the certificate of incorporation contains a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation`
    AND `s 343(2) the certificate of incorporation contains the provisions required by s 342` certificate

§§ `s 344 Election of existing corporation to become a close corporation`

-- The vote: "the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are
-- outstanding". fork F10: every class counts, including a class that does not otherwise vote.
-- src:1703 | Any corporation organized under this chapter may become a close corporation under this subchapter by executing, acknowledging and filing, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of amendment of its certificate of incorporation which shall contain a statement that it elects to become a close corporation, the provisions required by § 342 of this title to appear in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, and a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation. Such amendment shall be adopted in accordance with the requirements of § 241 or 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 344 (src:1703)
DECLARE `s 344 Class vote` HAS
    `the number of shares of the class that are outstanding, for the s 344 vote`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those shares held of record by the holders who approved, for the s 344 vote` IS A NUMBER

-- src:1703 | Any corporation organized under this chapter may become a close corporation under this subchapter by executing, acknowledging and filing, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of amendment of its certificate of incorporation which shall contain a statement that it elects to become a close corporation, the provisions required by § 342 of this title to appear in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, and a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation. Such amendment shall be adopted in accordance with the requirements of § 241 or 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 344 (src:1703)
GIVEN class IS A `s 344 Class vote`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344 the holders of at least 2/3 of the shares of the class approved` class MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`at least` (2 DIVIDED BY 3) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "the outstanding shares of the class")) (class's `the number of those shares held of record by the holders who approved, for the s 344 vote`) (class's `the number of shares of the class that are outstanding, for the s 344 vote`)

-- Every class must approve. A class whose counts cannot be a vote is not covered (NOTHING); NOTHING is never turned
-- into FALSE, but a class that plainly did not approve decides the matter whatever the others are.
-- (Also used by s 346(a).)
-- src:1703 | Any corporation organized under this chapter may become a close corporation under this subchapter by executing, acknowledging and filing, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of amendment of its certificate of incorporation which shall contain a statement that it elects to become a close corporation, the provisions required by § 342 of this title to appear in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, and a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation. Such amendment shall be adopted in accordance with the requirements of § 241 or 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 344 (src:1703)
GIVEN results IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344 every class vote carries` results MEANS
    CONSIDER results
    WHEN EMPTY THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER first
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            (CONSIDER `s 344 every class vote carries` rest
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
             WHEN JUST others THEN (IF others THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE))
        WHEN JUST this THEN (IF this THEN `s 344 every class vote carries` rest ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:1703 | Any corporation organized under this chapter may become a close corporation under this subchapter by executing, acknowledging and filing, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of amendment of its certificate of incorporation which shall contain a statement that it elects to become a close corporation, the provisions required by § 342 of this title to appear in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, and a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation. Such amendment shall be adopted in accordance with the requirements of § 241 or 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 344 (src:1703)
GIVEN classes IS A LIST OF `s 344 Class vote`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344 the holders of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class approved` classes MEANS
    CONSIDER classes
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE `s 344 every class vote carries` (map (GIVEN class YIELD `s 344 the holders of at least 2/3 of the shares of the class approved` class) classes)

-- src:1703 | Any corporation organized under this chapter may become a close corporation under this subchapter by executing, acknowledging and filing, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of amendment of its certificate of incorporation which shall contain a statement that it elects to become a close corporation, the provisions required by § 342 of this title to appear in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, and a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation. Such amendment shall be adopted in accordance with the requirements of § 241 or 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 344 (src:1703)
DECLARE `s 344 Election to become a close corporation` HAS
    `the corporation is organized under this chapter`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of amendment contains a statement that the corporation elects to become a close corporation`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of amendment contains the provisions required by s 342 to appear in the certificate of a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of amendment contains a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate of amendment was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103`                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
    `the amendment was adopted in accordance with the requirements of s 241 or s 242`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: sections 241 and 242 (piece dg5)

-- A corporation that has not done all this has not become a close corporation (JUST FALSE); one that has is a
-- close corporation if each class approved, which may be not covered (NOTHING) if a class's counts are not a vote.
-- src:1703 | Any corporation organized under this chapter may become a close corporation under this subchapter by executing, acknowledging and filing, in accordance with § 103 of this title, a certificate of amendment of its certificate of incorporation which shall contain a statement that it elects to become a close corporation, the provisions required by § 342 of this title to appear in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, and a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation. Such amendment shall be adopted in accordance with the requirements of § 241 or 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 344 (src:1703)
GIVEN election IS A `s 344 Election to become a close corporation`
      classes IS A LIST OF `s 344 Class vote`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344 the corporation has become a close corporation by election` election classes MEANS
    IF        election's `the corporation is organized under this chapter`
          AND election's `the certificate of amendment contains a statement that the corporation elects to become a close corporation`
          AND election's `the certificate of amendment contains the provisions required by s 342 to appear in the certificate of a close corporation`
          AND election's `the certificate of amendment contains a heading stating the name of the corporation and that it is a close corporation`
          AND election's `the certificate of amendment was executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103`
          AND election's `the amendment was adopted in accordance with the requirements of s 241 or s 242`
    THEN `s 344 the holders of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class approved` classes
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 345 Limitations on continuation of close corporation status`

-- src:1707 | A close corporation continues to be such and to be subject to this subchapter until:
-- src:1708 | (1) It files with the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment deleting from its certificate of incorporation the provisions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in the certificate of incorporation to qualify it as a close corporation; or
-- src:1709 | (2) Any 1 of the provisions or conditions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in a certificate of incorporation to qualify a corporation as a close corporation has in fact been breached and neither the corporation nor any of its stockholders takes the steps required by § 348 of this title to prevent such loss of status or to remedy such breach.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 345 (src:1707-1709)
GIVEN `the corporation is a close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation filed with the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment deleting the provisions required or permitted by s 342` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision or condition required or permitted by s 342 has in fact been breached` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation or a stockholder took the steps required by s 348 to prevent the loss of status or to remedy the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 345 the corporation continues to be a close corporation` `the corporation is a close corporation` `the corporation filed with the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment deleting the provisions required or permitted by s 342` `a provision or condition required or permitted by s 342 has in fact been breached` `the corporation or a stockholder took the steps required by s 348 to prevent the loss of status or to remedy the breach` MEANS
        `the corporation is a close corporation`
    AND (NOT `the corporation filed with the Secretary of State a certificate of amendment deleting the provisions required or permitted by s 342`)
    AND (NOT (    `a provision or condition required or permitted by s 342 has in fact been breached`
              AND (NOT `the corporation or a stockholder took the steps required by s 348 to prevent the loss of status or to remedy the breach`)))

§§ `s 346 Voluntary termination of close corporation status by amendment of certificate of incorporation; vote required`

-- (a): at least 2/3 of the shares of each class outstanding; (b): the certificate may require a greater vote, or a
-- vote of all shares of any class, and that provision cannot be amended, repealed or modified by a smaller vote.
-- src:1713 | (a) A corporation may voluntarily terminate its status as a close corporation and cease to be subject to this subchapter by amending its certificate of incorporation to delete therefrom the additional provisions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation. Any such amendment shall be adopted and shall become effective in accordance with § 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
-- src:1714 | (b) The certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that on any amendment to terminate its status as a close corporation, a vote greater than 2/3 or a vote of all shares of any class shall be required; and if the certificate of incorporation contains such a provision, that provision shall not be amended, repealed or modified by any vote less than that required to terminate the corporation’s status as a close corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 346(a) (src:1713); § 346(b) (src:1714)
DECLARE `s 346 Class vote` HAS
    `the number of shares of the class that are outstanding, for the s 346 vote`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those shares held of record by the holders who approved, for the s 346 vote` IS A NUMBER
    `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- The proportion needed is 2/3, or the greater proportion the certificate requires (up to all the shares of the
-- class). A figure in the certificate below 2/3 is not a greater vote and does not lower the 2/3.
-- src:1714 | (b) The certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that on any amendment to terminate its status as a close corporation, a vote greater than 2/3 or a vote of all shares of any class shall be required; and if the certificate of incorporation contains such a provision, that provision shall not be amended, repealed or modified by any vote less than that required to terminate the corporation’s status as a close corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 346(b) (src:1714)
GIVEN `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 346(b) the proportion of the class required to terminate close corporation status` `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 2 DIVIDED BY 3
    WHEN JUST required THEN (IF required GREATER THAN (2 DIVIDED BY 3) THEN required ELSE 2 DIVIDED BY 3)

-- "that provision shall not be amended, repealed or modified by any vote less than that required to terminate the
-- corporation's status as a close corporation": the same proportion.
-- src:1714 | (b) The certificate of incorporation of a close corporation may provide that on any amendment to terminate its status as a close corporation, a vote greater than 2/3 or a vote of all shares of any class shall be required; and if the certificate of incorporation contains such a provision, that provision shall not be amended, repealed or modified by any vote less than that required to terminate the corporation’s status as a close corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 346(b) (src:1714)
GIVEN `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 346(b) the proportion of the class required to amend, repeal or modify the greater-vote provision` `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one` MEANS
    `s 346(b) the proportion of the class required to terminate close corporation status` `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one`

-- src:1713 | (a) A corporation may voluntarily terminate its status as a close corporation and cease to be subject to this subchapter by amending its certificate of incorporation to delete therefrom the additional provisions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation. Any such amendment shall be adopted and shall become effective in accordance with § 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 346(a) (src:1713)
GIVEN class IS A `s 346 Class vote`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(a) the holders of the required proportion of the shares of the class approved the amendment` class MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`at least` (`s 346(b) the proportion of the class required to terminate close corporation status` (class's `the greater proportion of the class that the certificate of incorporation requires, if it requires one`)) `of` (`another base named in the provision` "the outstanding shares of the class")) (class's `the number of those shares held of record by the holders who approved, for the s 346 vote`) (class's `the number of shares of the class that are outstanding, for the s 346 vote`)

-- src:1713 | (a) A corporation may voluntarily terminate its status as a close corporation and cease to be subject to this subchapter by amending its certificate of incorporation to delete therefrom the additional provisions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation. Any such amendment shall be adopted and shall become effective in accordance with § 242 of this title, except that it must be approved by a vote of the holders of record of at least 2/3 of the shares of each class of stock of the corporation which are outstanding.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 346(a) (src:1713)
GIVEN classes IS A LIST OF `s 346 Class vote`
      `the amendment was adopted and became effective in accordance with s 242` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 242 (piece dg5)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(a) the corporation has voluntarily terminated its close corporation status` classes `the amendment was adopted and became effective in accordance with s 242` MEANS
    IF `the amendment was adopted and became effective in accordance with s 242`
    THEN (CONSIDER classes
          WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
          OTHERWISE `s 344 every class vote carries` (map (GIVEN class YIELD `s 346(a) the holders of the required proportion of the shares of the class approved the amendment` class) classes))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 347 Issuance or transfer of stock of a close corporation in breach of qualifying conditions`

-- (a): a transferee who is not entitled to be a holder of record, if the stock certificate conspicuously notes the
-- qualifications, is conclusively presumed to have notice of the ineligibility.
-- src:1718 | (a) If stock of a close corporation is issued or transferred to any person who is not entitled under any provision of the certificate of incorporation permitted by § 342(b) of this title to be a holder of record of stock of such corporation, and if the certificate for such stock conspicuously notes the qualifications of the persons entitled to be holders of record thereof, such person is conclusively presumed to have notice of the fact of such person’s ineligibility to be a stockholder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 347(a) (src:1718)
GIVEN `the person to whom the stock was issued or transferred is not entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stock certificate conspicuously notes the qualifications of the persons entitled to be holders of record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 347(a) the transferee is conclusively presumed to have notice of the transferee's ineligibility` `the person to whom the stock was issued or transferred is not entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record` `the stock certificate conspicuously notes the qualifications of the persons entitled to be holders of record` MEANS
        `the person to whom the stock was issued or transferred is not entitled under the certificate of incorporation to be a holder of record`
    AND `the stock certificate conspicuously notes the qualifications of the persons entitled to be holders of record`

-- (b): the certificate states the number of persons (not in excess of 30) entitled to be holders of record, the stock
-- certificate conspicuously states that number, and the issuance or transfer would put the stock in more hands.
-- src:1719 | (b) If the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation states the number of persons, not in excess of 30, who are entitled to be holders of record of its stock, and if the certificate for such stock conspicuously states such number, and if the issuance or transfer of stock to any person would cause the stock to be held by more than such number of persons, the person to whom such stock is issued or transferred is conclusively presumed to have notice of this fact.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 347(b) (src:1719)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation states a number of persons entitled to be holders of record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons the certificate states` IS A NUMBER
      `the stock certificate conspicuously states that number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of persons who would hold the stock after the issuance or transfer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 347(b) the transferee is conclusively presumed to have notice that the stock would be held by more than the stated number of persons` `the certificate of incorporation states a number of persons entitled to be holders of record` `the number of persons the certificate states` `the stock certificate conspicuously states that number` `the number of persons who would hold the stock after the issuance or transfer` MEANS
        `the certificate of incorporation states a number of persons entitled to be holders of record`
    AND `the number of persons the certificate states` AT MOST 30
    AND `the stock certificate conspicuously states that number`
    AND `the number of persons who would hold the stock after the issuance or transfer` GREATER THAN `the number of persons the certificate states`

-- (c): a restriction on transfer permitted by s 202, conspicuously noted on the stock certificate, and violated.
-- src:1720 | (c) If a stock certificate of any close corporation conspicuously notes the fact of a restriction on transfer of stock of the corporation, and the restriction is one which is permitted by § 202 of this title, the transferee of the stock is conclusively presumed to have notice of the fact that such person has acquired stock in violation of the restriction, if such acquisition violates the restriction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 347(c) (src:1720)
GIVEN `the stock certificate conspicuously notes the fact of a restriction on transfer of stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the restriction is one permitted by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 202 (piece dg3)
      `the acquisition violates the restriction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 347(c) the transferee is conclusively presumed to have notice that the stock was acquired in violation of the restriction` `the stock certificate conspicuously notes the fact of a restriction on transfer of stock` `the restriction is one permitted by s 202` `the acquisition violates the restriction` MEANS
        `the stock certificate conspicuously notes the fact of a restriction on transfer of stock`
    AND `the restriction is one permitted by s 202`
    AND `the acquisition violates the restriction`

-- (e): subsection (d) does not apply if all the stockholders consented to the transfer, or the corporation has
-- amended its certificate of incorporation in accordance with s 346.
-- src:1726 | (e) Subsection (d) of this section shall not be applicable if the transfer of stock, even though otherwise contrary to subsection (a), (b) or (c) of this section has been consented to by all the stockholders of the close corporation, or if the close corporation has amended its certificate of incorporation in accordance with § 346 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 347(e) (src:1726)
GIVEN `all the stockholders of the close corporation have consented to the transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the close corporation has amended its certificate of incorporation in accordance with s 346` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 347(e) subsection (d) does not apply` `all the stockholders of the close corporation have consented to the transfer` `the close corporation has amended its certificate of incorporation in accordance with s 346` MEANS
        `all the stockholders of the close corporation have consented to the transfer`
    OR  `the close corporation has amended its certificate of incorporation in accordance with s 346`

-- (d): "the corporation may, at its option, refuse to register transfer of the stock into the name of the
-- transferee": a permission, not a duty (fork F11).
-- src:1721 | (d) Whenever any person to whom stock of a close corporation has been issued or transferred has, or is conclusively presumed under this section to have, notice either:
-- src:1722 | (1) That such person is a person not eligible to be a holder of stock of the corporation, or
-- src:1723 | (2) That transfer of stock to such person would cause the stock of the corporation to be held by more than the number of persons permitted by its certificate of incorporation to hold stock of the corporation, or
-- src:1724 | (3) That the transfer of stock is in violation of a restriction on transfer of stock,
-- src:1725 | the corporation may, at its option, refuse to register transfer of the stock into the name of the transferee.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 347(d) (src:1721-1725)
GIVEN `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transferee is not eligible to be a holder of stock of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transfer would cause the stock to be held by more than the number of persons permitted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transfer of stock is in violation of a restriction on transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (e) makes subsection (d) inapplicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 347(d) the corporation may refuse to register the transfer of the stock into the name of the transferee` `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transferee is not eligible to be a holder of stock of the corporation` `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transfer would cause the stock to be held by more than the number of persons permitted` `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transfer of stock is in violation of a restriction on transfer` `subsection (e) makes subsection (d) inapplicable` MEANS
        (    `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transferee is not eligible to be a holder of stock of the corporation`
         OR  `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transfer would cause the stock to be held by more than the number of persons permitted`
         OR  `the transferee has, or is conclusively presumed to have, notice that the transfer of stock is in violation of a restriction on transfer`)
    AND (NOT `subsection (e) makes subsection (d) inapplicable`)

-- src:1727 | (f) The term “transfer,” as used in this section, is not limited to a transfer for value.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 347(f) (src:1727)
GIVEN `stock of the close corporation has been issued or transferred, whether or not for value` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 347(f) the issuance or transfer, whether or not for value, is a transfer for the purposes of s 347` `stock of the close corporation has been issued or transferred, whether or not for value` MEANS
    `stock of the close corporation has been issued or transferred, whether or not for value`

-- src:1728 | (g) The provisions of this section do not in any way impair any rights of a transferee regarding any right to rescind the transaction or to recover under any applicable warranty express or implied.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 347(g) (src:1728)
GIVEN `the transferee has a right under other law to rescind the transaction or to recover under an express or implied warranty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(g) the section impairs the transferee's right to rescind the transaction or to recover under a warranty` `the transferee has a right under other law to rescind the transaction or to recover under an express or implied warranty` MEANS
    IF `the transferee has a right under other law to rescind the transaction or to recover under an express or implied warranty`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 348 Involuntary termination of close corporation status; proceeding to prevent loss of status`

-- (a)(1): "Within 30 days after the occurrence of the event, or within 30 days after the event has been discovered,
-- whichever is later". The 30th day is inside the period (fork F1).
-- src:1733 | (1) Within 30 days after the occurrence of the event, or within 30 days after the event has been discovered, whichever is later, the corporation files with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, stating that a specified provision or condition included in its certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 342 of this title to qualify it as a close corporation has ceased to be applicable, and furnishes a copy of such certificate to each stockholder; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(a)(1) (src:1733)
GIVEN event IS A DATE
      discovered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 348(a)(1) the later of 30 days after the event and 30 days after its discovery` event discovered MEANS
    IF (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` discovered) AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` event)
    THEN `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` discovered
    ELSE `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` event

-- An event not yet discovered: the last day is not yet fixed (not covered, NOTHING).
-- src:1733 | (1) Within 30 days after the occurrence of the event, or within 30 days after the event has been discovered, whichever is later, the corporation files with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, stating that a specified provision or condition included in its certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 342 of this title to qualify it as a close corporation has ceased to be applicable, and furnishes a copy of such certificate to each stockholder; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(a)(1) (src:1733)
GIVEN `the date the event occurred` IS A DATE
      `the date the event was discovered, if it has been discovered` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 348(a)(1) the last day for the corporation to file the certificate` `the date the event occurred` `the date the event was discovered, if it has been discovered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the event was discovered, if it has been discovered`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST found THEN JUST (`s 348(a)(1) the later of 30 days after the event and 30 days after its discovery` `the date the event occurred` found)

-- src:1733 | (1) Within 30 days after the occurrence of the event, or within 30 days after the event has been discovered, whichever is later, the corporation files with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, stating that a specified provision or condition included in its certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 342 of this title to qualify it as a close corporation has ceased to be applicable, and furnishes a copy of such certificate to each stockholder; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(a)(1) (src:1733)
DECLARE `s 348(a) Steps taken after a breach` HAS
    `the date the event occurred`                                                                                   IS A DATE
    `the date the event was discovered, if it has been discovered`                                                  IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date the certificate was filed with the Secretary of State`                                               IS A DATE
    `the certificate states that a specified provision or condition has ceased to be applicable`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103`                                       IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
    `a copy of the certificate was furnished to each stockholder`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation took the steps necessary to correct the situation on the date the certificate was filed`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- (a)(1): filed with the Secretary of State in time, with a statement, executed and acknowledged, and a copy
-- furnished to each stockholder. When the discovery date is not known the time limit cannot be applied (NOTHING),
-- unless another condition plainly fails.
-- src:1733 | (1) Within 30 days after the occurrence of the event, or within 30 days after the event has been discovered, whichever is later, the corporation files with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, stating that a specified provision or condition included in its certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 342 of this title to qualify it as a close corporation has ceased to be applicable, and furnishes a copy of such certificate to each stockholder; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(a)(1) (src:1733)
GIVEN steps IS A `s 348(a) Steps taken after a breach`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348(a)(1) the corporation filed the certificate in time and furnished a copy to each stockholder` steps MEANS
    IF        steps's `the certificate states that a specified provision or condition has ceased to be applicable`
          AND steps's `the certificate was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103`
          AND steps's `a copy of the certificate was furnished to each stockholder`
    THEN (CONSIDER `s 348(a)(1) the last day for the corporation to file the certificate` (steps's `the date the event occurred`) (steps's `the date the event was discovered, if it has been discovered`)
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
          WHEN JUST lastDay THEN JUST ((steps's `the date the certificate was filed with the Secretary of State`) AT MOST lastDay))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:1734 | (2) The corporation concurrently with the filing of such certificate takes such steps as are necessary to correct the situation which threatens its status as a close corporation, including, without limitation, the refusal to register the transfer of stock which has been wrongfully transferred as provided by § 347 of this title, or a proceeding under subsection (b) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(a)(2) (src:1734)
GIVEN steps IS A `s 348(a) Steps taken after a breach`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(a)(2) the corporation concurrently took the steps necessary to correct the situation` steps MEANS
    steps's `the corporation took the steps necessary to correct the situation on the date the certificate was filed`

-- (a): the status terminates unless (1) and (2) (cumulative; fork F12).
-- src:1732 | (a) If any event occurs as a result of which 1 or more of the provisions or conditions included in a close corporation’s certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 342 of this title to qualify it as a close corporation has been breached, the corporation’s status as a close corporation under this subchapter shall terminate unless:
-- src:1733 | (1) Within 30 days after the occurrence of the event, or within 30 days after the event has been discovered, whichever is later, the corporation files with the Secretary of State a certificate, executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, stating that a specified provision or condition included in its certificate of incorporation pursuant to § 342 of this title to qualify it as a close corporation has ceased to be applicable, and furnishes a copy of such certificate to each stockholder; and
-- src:1734 | (2) The corporation concurrently with the filing of such certificate takes such steps as are necessary to correct the situation which threatens its status as a close corporation, including, without limitation, the refusal to register the transfer of stock which has been wrongfully transferred as provided by § 347 of this title, or a proceeding under subsection (b) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(a) (src:1732-1734)
GIVEN steps IS A `s 348(a) Steps taken after a breach`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348(a) the corporation's status as a close corporation survives the breach` steps MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 348(a)(1) the corporation filed the certificate in time and furnished a copy to each stockholder` steps
    WHEN NOTHING THEN (IF `s 348(a)(2) the corporation concurrently took the steps necessary to correct the situation` steps THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE)
    WHEN JUST inTime THEN JUST (inTime AND `s 348(a)(2) the corporation concurrently took the steps necessary to correct the situation` steps)

-- (b): on the suit of the corporation or a stockholder the Court of Chancery has jurisdiction to issue all orders
-- necessary to prevent loss of status or restore it; it may enjoin or set aside a transfer contrary to the certificate
-- or a s 202 restriction, and enjoin any public offering or threatened public offering (fork F13: the suit
-- condition is read as governing all three).
-- src:1735 | (b) The Court of Chancery, upon the suit of the corporation or any stockholder, shall have jurisdiction to issue all orders necessary to prevent the corporation from losing its status as a close corporation, or to restore its status as a close corporation by enjoining or setting aside any act or threatened act on the part of the corporation or a stockholder which would be inconsistent with any of the provisions or conditions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, unless it is an act approved in accordance with § 346 of this title. The Court of Chancery may enjoin or set aside any transfer or threatened transfer of stock of a close corporation which is contrary to the terms of its certificate of incorporation or of any transfer restriction permitted by § 202 of this title, and may enjoin any public offering, as defined in § 342 of this title, or threatened public offering of stock of the close corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(b) (src:1735)
GIVEN `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act or threatened act is inconsistent with a provision or condition required or permitted by s 342` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act was approved in accordance with s 346` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(b) the Court of Chancery has jurisdiction to issue orders to prevent loss of close corporation status or to restore it` `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder` `the act or threatened act is inconsistent with a provision or condition required or permitted by s 342` `the act was approved in accordance with s 346` MEANS
        `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder`
    AND `the act or threatened act is inconsistent with a provision or condition required or permitted by s 342`
    AND (NOT `the act was approved in accordance with s 346`)

-- src:1735 | (b) The Court of Chancery, upon the suit of the corporation or any stockholder, shall have jurisdiction to issue all orders necessary to prevent the corporation from losing its status as a close corporation, or to restore its status as a close corporation by enjoining or setting aside any act or threatened act on the part of the corporation or a stockholder which would be inconsistent with any of the provisions or conditions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, unless it is an act approved in accordance with § 346 of this title. The Court of Chancery may enjoin or set aside any transfer or threatened transfer of stock of a close corporation which is contrary to the terms of its certificate of incorporation or of any transfer restriction permitted by § 202 of this title, and may enjoin any public offering, as defined in § 342 of this title, or threatened public offering of stock of the close corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(b) (src:1735)
GIVEN `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer or threatened transfer is contrary to the terms of the certificate of incorporation or of a transfer restriction permitted by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(b) the Court of Chancery may enjoin or set aside the transfer or threatened transfer of stock` `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder` `the transfer or threatened transfer is contrary to the terms of the certificate of incorporation or of a transfer restriction permitted by s 202` MEANS
        `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder`
    AND `the transfer or threatened transfer is contrary to the terms of the certificate of incorporation or of a transfer restriction permitted by s 202`

-- src:1735 | (b) The Court of Chancery, upon the suit of the corporation or any stockholder, shall have jurisdiction to issue all orders necessary to prevent the corporation from losing its status as a close corporation, or to restore its status as a close corporation by enjoining or setting aside any act or threatened act on the part of the corporation or a stockholder which would be inconsistent with any of the provisions or conditions required or permitted by § 342 of this title to be stated in the certificate of incorporation of a close corporation, unless it is an act approved in accordance with § 346 of this title. The Court of Chancery may enjoin or set aside any transfer or threatened transfer of stock of a close corporation which is contrary to the terms of its certificate of incorporation or of any transfer restriction permitted by § 202 of this title, and may enjoin any public offering, as defined in § 342 of this title, or threatened public offering of stock of the close corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 348(b) (src:1735)
GIVEN `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a public offering, as defined in s 342, or a threatened public offering of stock of the close corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(b) the Court of Chancery may enjoin the public offering or threatened public offering of stock` `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder` `there is a public offering, as defined in s 342, or a threatened public offering of stock of the close corporation` MEANS
        `the suit is by the corporation or a stockholder`
    AND `there is a public offering, as defined in s 342, or a threatened public offering of stock of the close corporation`

§§ `s 349 Corporate option where a restriction on transfer of a security is held invalid`

-- "for a period of 30 days after the judgment setting aside the restriction becomes final": the 30th day is inside.
-- src:1739 | If a restriction on transfer of a security of a close corporation is held not to be authorized by § 202 of this title, the corporation shall nevertheless have an option, for a period of 30 days after the judgment setting aside the restriction becomes final, to acquire the restricted security at a price which is agreed upon by the parties, or if no agreement is reached as to price, then at the fair value as determined by the Court of Chancery. In order to determine fair value, the Court may appoint an appraiser to receive evidence and report to the Court such appraiser’s findings and recommendation as to fair value.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 349 (src:1739)
GIVEN `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 349 the last day of the corporation's option to acquire the restricted security` `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final`

-- src:1739 | If a restriction on transfer of a security of a close corporation is held not to be authorized by § 202 of this title, the corporation shall nevertheless have an option, for a period of 30 days after the judgment setting aside the restriction becomes final, to acquire the restricted security at a price which is agreed upon by the parties, or if no agreement is reached as to price, then at the fair value as determined by the Court of Chancery. In order to determine fair value, the Court may appoint an appraiser to receive evidence and report to the Court such appraiser’s findings and recommendation as to fair value.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 349 (src:1739)
GIVEN `a restriction on transfer of a security of a close corporation is held not to be authorized by s 202` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 202 (piece dg3)
      `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final` IS A DATE
      `the date the option is exercised` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 349 the corporation may still exercise its option to acquire the restricted security` `a restriction on transfer of a security of a close corporation is held not to be authorized by s 202` `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final` `the date the option is exercised` MEANS
        `a restriction on transfer of a security of a close corporation is held not to be authorized by s 202`
    AND `the date the option is exercised` AT LEAST `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final`
    AND `the date the option is exercised` AT MOST (`s 349 the last day of the corporation's option to acquire the restricted security` `the date the judgment setting aside the restriction became final`)

-- "at a price which is agreed upon by the parties, or if no agreement is reached as to price, then at the fair value
-- as determined by the Court of Chancery". Until one of them exists the price is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:1739 | If a restriction on transfer of a security of a close corporation is held not to be authorized by § 202 of this title, the corporation shall nevertheless have an option, for a period of 30 days after the judgment setting aside the restriction becomes final, to acquire the restricted security at a price which is agreed upon by the parties, or if no agreement is reached as to price, then at the fair value as determined by the Court of Chancery. In order to determine fair value, the Court may appoint an appraiser to receive evidence and report to the Court such appraiser’s findings and recommendation as to fair value.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 349 (src:1739)
GIVEN `the price agreed upon by the parties, if the parties agreed one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the fair value determined by the Court of Chancery, if it has determined one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 349 the price at which the corporation may acquire the restricted security` `the price agreed upon by the parties, if the parties agreed one` `the fair value determined by the Court of Chancery, if it has determined one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the price agreed upon by the parties, if the parties agreed one`
    WHEN JUST agreed THEN JUST agreed
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the fair value determined by the Court of Chancery, if it has determined one`
